From f19e703c5d2dc14cbc151ddbbbfb8ba411f36192 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Suresh, Prashanth" <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:43:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media-driver: Add missing gen11_icllp/vp/kernel include dir

A real flashfiles build failed with a fatal file-not-found error:
vphal_renderer_g11_icllp.cpp includes "igvpkrn_g11_icllp.h", whose
containing directory, media_driver/agnostic/gen11_icllp/vp/kernel, was
excluded from the earlier comprehensive include-dirs sweep alongside
its kernel_free sibling as a 'legacy generation-specific kernel source
duplicate'.

That exclusion was too broad: the kernel/ (not kernel_free/) copy is
the one whose .c sources (igvpkrn_g11_icllp.c,
igvpkrn_isa_g11_icllp.c) are actually compiled per Android.bp's srcs
list, so its headers are load-bearing, not dead legacy code. Added
only media_driver/agnostic/gen11_icllp/vp/kernel (not kernel_free,
which remains genuinely unused and excluded) -- avoids the
Source/Source duplicate filename ambiguity entirely by picking the
directory that matches the compiled sources.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1547
Signed-off-by: Suresh, Prashanth <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
---
 Android.bp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 1f1037954..2c8f867b9 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -2450,6 +2450,7 @@ cc_library_shared {
         "media_driver/agnostic/gen11/renderhal",
         "media_driver/agnostic/gen11/vp/hal",
         "media_driver/agnostic/gen11_icllp/vp/hal",
+        "media_driver/agnostic/gen11_icllp/vp/kernel",
         "media_driver/agnostic/gen11_jsl_ehl/renderhal",
         "media_driver/agnostic/gen11_jsl_ehl/vp/hal",
         "media_driver/agnostic/gen12",
-- 
2.34.1

